  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 7-Angeloylechinatine and the CD276 antigen, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. The drug is predicted to interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is targeted by 3-(1H-Benzimidazol-2-Yl)-7-(Diethylamino)Chromen-2-One and (S)-2-Methylbutanoate. These compounds, in turn, target the CD276 antigen. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent pattern of interaction, with slight variations in confidence scores, likely due to differences in the specific targets and their binding affinities. The evidence supports a pathway where 7-Angeloylechinatine acts as a modulator of the CD276 antigen through a series of phosphatase-mediated interactions. The mechanism involves the regulation of signaling pathways that are associated with immune responses and tumor suppression, suggesting a possible role in immunotherapy. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple independent paths, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
